WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.450
Order pizza tonight and you
could probably choose from a long

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.700
list of restaurants in your town.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.290
Now try choosing who runs the
power lines to your house.

4
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:12.690
In most US towns, one utility owns them.

5
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.050
A wheat farmer has a different problem.

6
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.460
Charge even a cent above the market price,

7
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.470
and she sells nothing.

8
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.260
Why do some markets have
thousands of sellers while

9
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.140
others have only one or two?

10
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.310
In this mission, you'll line
up four market structures,

11
00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.690
from countless identical
sellers to just one.

12
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.950
Then you'll compare a
firm that has to take

13
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.350
the market price with one
that gets to set its own.

14
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:39.760
Your mission: find out what
decides how many sellers

15
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.910
a market can hold.
